{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011CeuCLDDszshnMdVJ9BS9h","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ScNpRgnYhgcZTovRKg8szV","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/bear/Documents/CoWork/bear-textbooks/books/anthropics/claude-code-101/03-hooks-skills-commands/cc-pretooluse-grade-blocker/scratch/summary.md","content":"# Student Summaries\n\n## Ada\nAda posted strong marks across the board — 92 on Quiz 1, 88 on Quiz 2, and a 90 on the project — with a perfect 10/10 attendance record. Her scores cluster tightly in the high 80s to low 90s, suggesting consistent preparation rather than a single lucky result, and her flawless attendance reinforces that steady work ethic.\n**Overall performance:** Excellent — top of the group. Suggested letter grade: **A-**\n\n## Boris\nBoris turned in the weakest quiz scores of the group (71 and 74) but recovered somewhat on the project with an 80, and his attendance was 8/10. The gap between his quiz and project performance hints that he does better with time to work than under timed conditions, and the two missed sessions may be a contributing factor worth a check-in.\n**Overall performance:** Below average — passing but with real room to grow. Suggested letter grade: **C**\n\n## Cai\nCai scored 84 on Quiz 1, improved to 90 on Quiz 2, and delivered an 88 on the project, with 9/10 attendance. The upward trajectory across the two quizzes is a good sign, and his project score confirms he can carry that level of work into a larger deliverable.\n**Overall performance:** Strong and improving. Suggested letter grade: **B+**\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":219,"cache_read_input_tokens":34563,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":219},"output_tokens":13,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_av